### What is Debouncing?

Debouncing is a programming practice used to ensure that time-consuming tasks do not fire so often that they cripple the performance of a web page. It's a way of limiting the rate at which a function gets called.

A debounced function will only be executed after a certain amount of time has passed *without it being called again*.

